rification.json"} {"question" "q-114597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1/3}^{e}-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x){|}_{1/3}^{e}-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-{\\int }_{1/3}^{e}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-x{|}_{1/3}^{e}\\, \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3e)-(e-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+e-e+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =e\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/state.json" "file_sha256" "4aa38037df6f95a2eef424da3ef13af3ea5c2025f7c24df111c7a4d1febae3b9" "basis" 1324 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012554/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/ref